- netstat -a shows all active connections and listening ports on your system — basically every socket, whether it’s established, waiting, or listening.
  netstat → Displays network statistics.

Option -s → Prints protocol statistics.

It breaks down traffic by protocol (TCP, UDP, ICMP, IP) and shows:

Packets received/sent

Errors (like checksum errors, retransmissions)

Dropped packets

Connection resets or failures
